<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="37917" href="schedule/2022/fall/BADM/590/37917.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="BADM" href="schedule/2022/fall/BADM.xml">Business Administration</subject><course id="590" href="schedule/2022/fall/BADM/590.xml">Seminar in Business Admin</course></parents><sectionNumber>IS1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Machine Learning in Bus Res</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will meet in 4001 BIF.  The class explores the role of machine learning (ML) while studying business policy-related research questions. We will discuss academic papers related to both methods and applications. While the focus will be on ML applications in information systems research, we will also explore applications in other areas such as management, finance, and accounting. Students will be expected to work on a research proposal and preliminary analysis.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to PHD:Business Administrtn -UIUC.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>ARR</roomNumber><buildingName>Business Instructional Fac</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Pant" firstName="G">Pant, G</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>